        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Laws: U.S. law on state citizenship and residency\n- Cases: The Slaughter-House Cases (1873), United States v. Darby Lumber Co.\n- Topics: Civil rights law, government approval\n\nFacts:\n- The Slaughter-House Cases were decided in 1873.\n- The chunk states that a U.S. law says state citizenship and residency are flexible.\n- The chunk states that no government approval is required under that U.S. law.\n- The chunk states that the law was held consistently in 1873.\n- The chunk states that The Slaughter-House Cases and United States v. Darby Lumber Co. did not both involve civil rights law.",
